Fixed `maybe_select_related()` and `BaseTable.add_conditional_prefetch()` raising when asked to follow a field that is not a relation on the model being rendered, rather than skipping it as their contracts describe.
Fixed a 500 when selecting Object Type on the Advanced tab of the retention rule filter form. The field lookup maps a content type filter to a feature name and then to a small map of querysets, and retention rules were in neither, so the request that builds the field raised `KeyError`.
Fixed `ArchivedJobResult` registering itself as a custom field model. It mirrors `JobResult` field for field, including the column the feature registry detects custom field models by, so retained job results were offered in the custom field object type picker and `cleanup_custom_field_data()` streamed every retained row over the archive database and wrote to any holding an orphaned key. Retained history is immutable.
Fixed every retained page render warning that its table was misconfigured. Rendering a warm table over a retention mirror is deliberate, so the model mismatch django-tables2 reports is expected there and is no longer raised.
Fixed the REST API accepting a retention rule whose scope filter the target model's FilterSet rejects. The edit form already refused such a filter and truncation skipped the rule at run time, so a rule created through the API could sit in the list looking enabled while doing nothing. It is now refused wherever it is saved.
